SUMMARY: Joy in the Park
DESCRIPTION:Our community’s arts organization\, Jamii\, is bringing Joy i
 n the Park back to David Crombie Park on Saturday\, July 25\, from 6 PM t
 o 8 PM. The community is invited to join in.\n\nThis free outdoor event w
 ill bring music\, dance\, art activities\, and summer energy to the heart
  of The Esplanade. The evening will feature live samba music by Sambaê\, 
 an all-women samba band led by Aline Morales\, followed by a dance perfor
 mance by Lua Shayenne Dance Company\, with live percussion\, song\, movem
 ent\, and moments of audience participation rooted in African and Afro-di
 asporic traditions.\n\nFamilies and neighbours of all ages can also enjoy
  face painting\, henna\, crafts for kids\, complimentary coffee and tea\,
  a joyful stiltwalker\, and a slice of Jamii’s 15th Anniversary birthday 
 cake.\n\nChairs and blankets will be available\, and attendees are welcom
 e to bring their own.\n\nCome out for a warm summer evening of music\, mo
 vement\, and community connection in the park.\n\nFind more details at ww
 w.jamii.ca http://www.jamii.ca/\n\nFree.
